---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { classes } from '../../../styles';
---
<DocsLayout title="Tables, SVG, accessibility" description="Table layout, SVG presentation, and accessibility utilities."><header><p class={classes.eyebrow}>Utility reference</p><h1 class={classes.title}>Tables, SVG, accessibility</h1><p class={classes.lead}>Table layout, SVG presentation, and accessibility utilities.</p></header><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>Classes</h2><p class={classes.copy}>border-collapse, border-separate, border-spacing-*, table-auto, table-fixed, caption-top, caption-bottom, fill-*, stroke-*, stroke-cap-*, stroke-join-*, stroke-miterlimit-*, stroke-dasharray-*, stroke-dashoffset-*, fill-rule-*, clip-rule-*, vector-effect-*, paint-order-*, shape-rendering-*, sr-only, not-sr-only, and forced-color-adjust-*.</p></section><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>SVG presentation</h2><pre class={classes.code}><code>fill-current stroke-current stroke-cap-round stroke-join-round{`\n`}stroke-dasharray-[4_8] vector-effect-non-scaling-stroke paint-order-stroke</code></pre><p class={classes.copy}>Numeric stroke miter and dash utilities accept numbers. Use bracket values or custom properties for CSS values that contain units, spaces, or lists.</p></section></DocsLayout>
